WEBVTT

00:06.172 --> 00:07.424
[gunshots blasting]

00:11.386 --> 00:12.554
[blasting continues]

00:15.432 --> 00:17.434
- [exploding]
- [gunshots blasting]

00:18.017 --> 00:19.352
[clacking]

00:19.436 --> 00:21.187
[indistinct game voiceover]

00:21.271 --> 00:23.148
[gunshots blasting]

00:23.231 --> 00:25.150
[rapid-fire blasting]

00:28.319 --> 00:30.321
[loud rapid-fire blasting]

00:31.114 --> 00:33.116
[controller clacking]

00:35.910 --> 00:37.328
[rapid-fire blasting]

00:37.996 --> 00:39.914
[scraping]

00:39.998 --> 00:41.916
MAX VOLCANO

00:42.000 --> 00:44.419
FRACTAL GEOMETRY

00:44.502 --> 00:46.671
EVERYTHING ABOUT SACRED GEOMETRY

00:46.755 --> 00:48.673
AUDI AND BMW
3D GEOMETRY

00:48.757 --> 00:51.092
[rapid-fire blasting]

00:51.176 --> 00:52.260
[clacking]

00:52.343 --> 00:54.304
[rapid-fire blasting continues]

00:55.805 --> 00:57.640
[Hajime] You're a shitty brother.

00:57.724 --> 00:58.641
[splattering]

00:58.725 --> 00:59.559
Crap!

01:00.226 --> 01:01.102
[Arisu groans]

01:02.687 --> 01:03.605
[Arisu sucks teeth]

01:04.355 --> 01:06.483
[Hajime] You didn't go to the interview
I set up again?

01:10.195 --> 01:13.990
I begged the company for it.
You should really show up, for my sake.

01:16.076 --> 01:18.244
Did I ask you to go and set it up?
[scoffs]

01:19.370 --> 01:21.623
Dad said this is the last time
he's helping.

01:22.999 --> 01:25.418
He told me not to help you
look for a job anymore, either.

01:25.919 --> 01:28.463
[Arisu scoffs]
I never asked for your help.

01:28.546 --> 01:29.923
[Hajime] But you need it.

01:30.924 --> 01:32.675
You're a parasite in this house.

01:35.804 --> 01:37.013
[Arisu scoffs]
Fine, okay.

01:37.096 --> 01:38.473
[scoffs]
I'll leave then.

01:38.556 --> 01:39.390
[controller clanks]

01:39.474 --> 01:41.851
- If only we could reboot reality.
- [sighs]

01:44.854 --> 01:47.023
You were better when Mom was alive.

02:04.040 --> 02:05.250
Ryohei.

02:06.376 --> 02:08.878
I don't need you
causing trouble for your brother.

02:14.342 --> 02:16.344
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson playing]

02:16.427 --> 02:18.304
RESIDENCE

02:33.903 --> 02:37.323
CHOTA SEGAWA, DAIKICHI KARUBE

02:37.407 --> 02:38.324
[phone chimes]

02:38.408 --> 02:40.326
ARISU: CAN I GO TO THE BAR?

02:43.413 --> 02:44.664
[phone chimes]

02:44.747 --> 02:46.332
ARISU: I'M OFFICIALLY HOMELESS.

02:46.416 --> 02:48.585
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson playing]

02:53.381 --> 02:54.549
[smooching]

03:07.729 --> 03:08.688
[door opens]

03:08.771 --> 03:10.481
[breathes deeply]

03:11.441 --> 03:12.567
Oh, Mr. Boss, sir.

03:12.650 --> 03:14.277
- How are ya?
- Oh, it's Karube. You're in early today.

03:14.360 --> 03:15.945
Uh…
[clears throat]

03:16.029 --> 03:17.989
I just decided to come in a bit earlier.

03:18.072 --> 03:19.699
[Emi] Why are you here at this hour, Kazu?

03:19.782 --> 03:21.534
I have something to take care of.

03:22.118 --> 03:23.036
[Karube] Whoa!

03:23.119 --> 03:25.121
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson
continues playing]

03:26.956 --> 03:27.832
[song fades out]

03:27.916 --> 03:30.001
ARISU: KARUBE, YOU THERE?

03:31.127 --> 03:32.337
KARUBE

03:33.004 --> 03:33.963
[grunts]

03:34.505 --> 03:36.674
How dare you put your hands
on someone else's woman!

03:36.758 --> 03:38.426
[Emi squeals]
Stop it!

03:38.509 --> 03:40.094
Shut up, bitch!

03:40.678 --> 03:42.263
- [Karube grunts]
- [hard thumping]

03:42.347 --> 03:44.057
- [thuds]
- [breathes heavily]

03:44.140 --> 03:46.142
[pants]
I feel better now.

03:46.226 --> 03:48.228
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson
resumes playing]

03:48.311 --> 03:49.145
[chuckles]

03:58.863 --> 04:05.161
ARISU: CHOTA, YOU WORKING?
LET ME STAY OVER.

04:06.204 --> 04:07.121
[phone chimes]

04:07.205 --> 04:11.334
CHOTA

04:21.219 --> 04:22.136
[Chota] Here you go.

04:22.220 --> 04:23.096
Ah!

04:23.763 --> 04:26.599
I'm sorry that you have to do this
when you're so busy, Chota.

04:26.683 --> 04:29.560
This money will really help us out.

04:29.644 --> 04:31.562
Let's make this the last time, okay?

04:33.398 --> 04:35.358
- [Sayuri] What do you mean, the last time?
- [sighs]

04:36.776 --> 04:40.738
ARISU: HEY, ARE YOU GUYS IGNORING ME?

04:41.239 --> 04:43.283
[Sayuri] Don't you understand,
the air here in Tokyo

04:43.366 --> 04:45.994
is being polluted every day
by the powers of industry?

04:46.077 --> 04:48.621
[sighs]
We need to make it clean again!

04:48.705 --> 04:52.000
Here, here, there.
Everything has to be reclaimed!

04:52.083 --> 04:53.918
- Yeah, I get it already!
- [sighs]

04:54.002 --> 04:55.003
[exhales deeply]

04:55.086 --> 04:56.587
- I'm late.
- [Sayuri sighs]

04:56.671 --> 04:57.714
[Sayuri] Thank you!

04:57.797 --> 04:59.799
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson
continues playing]

05:01.259 --> 05:02.385
[inhales deeply]

05:03.052 --> 05:04.887
ARISU: FINE.

05:09.851 --> 05:11.394
[song fades]

05:11.477 --> 05:13.438
[upbeat music playing]

05:20.737 --> 05:23.740
KARUBE: I WAS FIRED FROM MY JOB.

05:23.823 --> 05:24.657
[exhales deeply]

05:26.659 --> 05:27.618
[Arisu groans]

05:28.202 --> 05:30.580
Karube's timing really sucks.

05:31.998 --> 05:33.458
ARISU: SERIOUSLY? WHEN?

05:33.541 --> 05:37.712
KARUBE: RIGHT NOW. I'M JOBLESS NOW!

05:37.795 --> 05:40.423
ARISU: SERIOUSLY? WHEN?
KARUBE: RIGHT NOW. I'M JOBLESS NOW!

05:40.506 --> 05:46.763
CHOTA: GOOD JOB GETTING FIRED.
I'M SKIPPING WORK RIGHT NOW.

05:48.097 --> 05:52.018
KARUBE: YOU SHOULD WORK, CHOTA.
YOU'RE POOR.

05:54.353 --> 05:56.481
ARISU: I LEFT HOME.

05:57.648 --> 05:59.358
CHOTA: GOOD WORK.

05:59.442 --> 06:01.360
ARISU: I NEED A DRINK.

06:01.444 --> 06:02.987
CHOTA: ME TOO!

06:03.071 --> 06:04.947
KARUBE: LET'S GO, THEN!

06:05.031 --> 06:07.950
ARISU: GO FIND A JOB, KARUBE.

06:08.034 --> 06:09.619
CHOTA: YOU TOO, ARISU.

06:09.702 --> 06:11.037
[chuckles]

06:11.120 --> 06:14.707
KARUBE: OKAY,
LET'S MEET IN FRONT OF SHIBUYA STATION.

06:14.791 --> 06:16.626
ARISU: OKAY!

06:16.709 --> 06:17.543
CHOTA: OKAY!

06:17.627 --> 06:18.544
Whoa!

06:19.754 --> 06:21.422
[groans]

06:21.506 --> 06:23.549
ARISU: I STEPPED ON SOMEONE'S VOMIT.

06:23.633 --> 06:26.094
CHOTA: GOOD JOB STEPPING ON VOMIT.

06:26.177 --> 06:28.179
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson
continues playing]

06:41.442 --> 06:44.612
ARISU: I'M HAVING THE WORST DAY.

06:45.613 --> 06:46.864
CHOTA: ME TOO.

06:46.948 --> 06:48.574
KARUBE: SAME.

06:48.658 --> 06:54.664
ARISU: I JUST DON'T FEEL LIKE I'VE BEEN
DOING MY BEST SINCE THIS MORNING.

06:56.541 --> 06:59.544
KARUBE:
ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT YOUR GAME?

07:03.256 --> 07:06.217
ARISU: FOUND YOU, KARUBE!

07:06.300 --> 07:07.969
FIND YOUR NEW SELF

07:08.052 --> 07:10.346
KARUBE: HEY!

07:10.429 --> 07:12.140
CHOTA: HEY!

07:12.223 --> 07:14.725
ARISU: HEY.

07:16.227 --> 07:17.478
Hey, we're right here.

07:17.562 --> 07:18.729
[all laugh]

07:18.813 --> 07:20.356
[Chota] You wanna go get a drink?

07:20.940 --> 07:23.109
It's early. Not many bars open.

07:23.192 --> 07:24.360
Man.

07:24.444 --> 07:25.695
[inhales sharply]

07:25.778 --> 07:28.156
That settles that,
guess we're going to a mall again.

07:29.449 --> 07:31.033
[inhales sharply]

07:32.243 --> 07:34.120
[Arisu groans]

07:34.203 --> 07:36.539
I'd be down with going to
a deserted island.

07:36.622 --> 07:37.457
[chuckles]

07:37.540 --> 07:39.542
[crowd chattering]

07:40.710 --> 07:43.546
I'd be down with zombies
showing up in Shibuya.

07:43.629 --> 07:46.340
Everyone here gets bitten,
and they all turn into zombies.

07:46.424 --> 07:48.885
Stop it with the zombie talk, will ya?

07:48.968 --> 07:52.013
If zombies did show up here,
only Karube would survive.

07:52.096 --> 07:54.515
- You'd knock 'em out with one punch.
- [chuckles]

07:54.599 --> 07:56.058
I doubt that.

07:56.142 --> 07:57.852
You'd be the one to survive, Arisu.

07:57.935 --> 07:59.437
Me? Why's that?

08:00.897 --> 08:03.065
Because I know you'd outsmart 'em.

08:06.861 --> 08:09.655
Arisu, free advice…

08:11.532 --> 08:14.577
You should stop hanging out with us
and go live your life.

08:16.370 --> 08:17.622
You should do it.

08:18.122 --> 08:19.123
[Karube puffs]

08:19.207 --> 08:20.374
Huh?

08:21.000 --> 08:22.335
[chuckles]
What's with him?

08:22.418 --> 08:24.378
[Arisu, Chota laugh]

08:25.087 --> 08:26.172
[Arisu scoffs]

08:36.474 --> 08:38.059
[breathes deeply]

08:44.232 --> 08:46.234
[mellow violin music]

09:15.304 --> 09:16.264
[exhales deeply]

09:16.347 --> 09:17.682
Shit, let's do this.

09:17.765 --> 09:18.766
- Come on!
- Whoa…

09:18.849 --> 09:20.893
- What are you doing?
- Whoa…

09:20.977 --> 09:22.728
This is the first day
of your independence!

09:22.812 --> 09:24.063
Shut up, take a picture!

09:24.146 --> 09:25.982
- [Chota] Okay!
- [Arisu] Oh…

09:26.065 --> 09:27.608
- [Karube] Comin' through!
- [Arisu] Whoa!

09:27.692 --> 09:28.943
- [Chota laughing]
- [Karube] Step aside!

09:29.026 --> 09:31.487
- Hey, this is dangerous!
- Give way!

09:31.571 --> 09:32.655
Hey, hey!

09:32.738 --> 09:35.157
[Chota] Hey, wait! Let me take a picture!

09:35.241 --> 09:36.158
[Karube] Whoa!

09:36.242 --> 09:37.702
[Arisu] Wait, what are you doing?

09:37.785 --> 09:38.828
[Chota] Turn towards me!

09:38.911 --> 09:40.788
Hey! Stop, no pictures!

09:40.871 --> 09:43.165
- Big smile, big smile!
- [Karube] Look here, look here!

09:43.249 --> 09:45.042
- [Arisu grunts]
- [Chota] Come on, Arisu!

09:45.126 --> 09:46.794
- Here, look at the camera!
- I'm sorry, everyone!…

09:46.877 --> 09:49.171
Stop, dammit! Fuck!

09:49.255 --> 09:51.841
[Chota chortles]
Now that's a good face!

09:51.924 --> 09:54.552
[pants, sighs]

09:55.553 --> 09:58.389
[crowd chattering]

10:04.478 --> 10:05.855
Oh…

10:05.938 --> 10:07.898
[high-pitched whooping]

10:07.982 --> 10:09.692
[chuckles]
That is perfect!

10:09.775 --> 10:11.569
[Arisu] Whoo!

10:11.652 --> 10:12.862
[Chota] Great!

10:12.945 --> 10:14.947
[cheering]

10:16.157 --> 10:19.493
[all hollering]

10:19.577 --> 10:21.203
Shibuya!

10:22.204 --> 10:23.748
You rock!

10:24.457 --> 10:26.000
[whooping]

10:26.083 --> 10:27.668
- [man 1] Oh, get off! Get off!
- [vehicle honks]

10:27.752 --> 10:29.170
[Arisu] Put me down. Whoa…

10:29.253 --> 10:30.796
- Come on. Quick, quick, quick.
- [grunts]

10:30.880 --> 10:33.466
- [man 2] You guys are crazy!
- [horn honks]

10:33.549 --> 10:35.134
- [all yelp]
- [white SUV honks]

10:35.217 --> 10:37.303
- Watch out! Look out!
- [white car beeps]

10:37.386 --> 10:38.846
- Hurry up!
- [all panting]

10:38.929 --> 10:40.097
[Chota] Look, fireworks!

10:40.181 --> 10:41.641
[Karube] Run for your lives!

10:41.724 --> 10:43.476
[vehicles beep]

10:43.559 --> 10:45.019
- [tires screech]
- [driver] Moron!

10:45.102 --> 10:46.604
- [crashing]
- [people scream]

10:46.687 --> 10:49.106
- [all panting]
- [Arisu] Guys, wa-- wait.

10:49.190 --> 10:50.274
It's the cops!

10:50.358 --> 10:52.193
- [Karube] Whoa! Go, go, go…
- [Arisu] We'll be in trouble!

10:52.276 --> 10:53.319
[Chota] Let's get out of here!

10:54.654 --> 10:55.863
[Karube] Run! Run!

10:55.946 --> 10:57.490
[people clamoring]

10:57.573 --> 11:00.242
[Arisu, Karube, Chota laughing]

11:01.702 --> 11:04.413
- [sighing in relief]
- [scanner beeps]

11:04.497 --> 11:05.956
- The stairs!
- [Karube] Yeah!

11:06.916 --> 11:08.751
- [Karube, Chota] Whoa!
- [Chota] Oh, watch out!

11:08.834 --> 11:10.920
- Head for the john!
- [Karube] Turn around! Turn around!

11:11.504 --> 11:12.713
- [Chota] Sorry!
- [Karube yelps]

11:12.797 --> 11:14.590
[all panting]

11:15.341 --> 11:17.218
[Karube] Go, go, go!

11:17.301 --> 11:18.969
[panting]

11:19.053 --> 11:20.429
- Let me lock it. Gimme a second.
- [Chota] Come on.

11:20.513 --> 11:23.015
- Just hurry it up, for fuck's sake!
- Damn!

11:23.099 --> 11:24.141
[Karube grunts]

11:24.225 --> 11:25.226
[panting]

11:26.811 --> 11:29.438
[all laughing]

11:34.735 --> 11:36.737
[Karube breathing heavily]

11:38.864 --> 11:40.741
CHOTA: WHO FARTED?

11:41.742 --> 11:43.744
[Arisu, Karube sniffing]

11:43.828 --> 11:46.622
[keypad tapping]

11:46.705 --> 11:49.458
CHOTA: WHO WAS IT?
OWN UP AND SNIFF UP YOUR OWN FART!

11:49.542 --> 11:51.544
[Chota giggles]

11:51.627 --> 11:53.129
[whispers]
It was you, right?

11:53.212 --> 11:54.922
[blowing playfully]

11:55.005 --> 11:56.715
[loud footsteps approaching]

11:57.633 --> 11:59.343
[knocking on door]

12:00.428 --> 12:03.305
[continuous knocking]

12:05.433 --> 12:06.892
[lights clunk]

12:14.400 --> 12:15.860
[Arisu] I don't hear anything.

12:32.293 --> 12:33.627
I'll go check it out.

12:33.711 --> 12:34.628
All right.

12:35.296 --> 12:37.214
- Be careful.
- Yeah, okay.

12:41.051 --> 12:42.136
[door clicks]

12:47.141 --> 12:48.767
[door creaks]

12:52.313 --> 12:53.314
[door closes]

14:08.806 --> 14:11.433
[ominous music]

14:30.703 --> 14:32.705
[papers rustling]

14:45.050 --> 14:47.052
[ominous music continues]

14:58.230 --> 15:00.232
[wind blowing]

15:29.511 --> 15:31.055
Jesus.

15:31.138 --> 15:34.016
[ominous music climaxes]

15:37.186 --> 15:39.188
[theme music]

16:47.631 --> 16:49.633
[eerie music]

17:08.652 --> 17:09.820
[sighs]

17:17.745 --> 17:18.662
Baby?

17:19.288 --> 17:21.123
[breathing heavily]

17:24.668 --> 17:25.753
Baby?

17:28.589 --> 17:30.841
[Chota panting]

17:39.767 --> 17:43.687
WHERE'S THE FILE?!
GET YOUR ACT TOGETHER!! - TAKAGI

17:43.771 --> 17:46.231
[breathing heavily]

17:56.241 --> 17:58.243
[eerie music]

18:06.335 --> 18:09.088
[eerie music crescendos]

18:24.228 --> 18:26.230
[soft music]

18:37.574 --> 18:40.119
[Arisu panting]

18:49.419 --> 18:51.421
[panting continues]

19:14.736 --> 19:16.613
[Arisu] What the fuck?

19:23.203 --> 19:25.205
[soft music]

19:32.212 --> 19:34.173
[distant crows cawing]

19:38.051 --> 19:40.053
[panting]

19:45.767 --> 19:47.144
[Arisu] Hey!

19:50.314 --> 19:51.690
Hello?

19:57.154 --> 19:58.614
Anyone there?

19:58.697 --> 20:00.949
[wind blows]

20:06.246 --> 20:07.539
Hello?

20:08.040 --> 20:10.042
[panting]

20:18.592 --> 20:20.594
[panting continues]

20:32.272 --> 20:33.398
Seen anyone?

20:33.482 --> 20:34.483
[Karube] No!

20:34.566 --> 20:35.943
[panting]

20:36.026 --> 20:37.110
[Arisu] See anybody?

20:37.736 --> 20:39.363
[Chota] There's no one anywhere!

20:39.446 --> 20:41.406
[all panting exasperatedly]

20:45.369 --> 20:47.746
[Arisu] Even my phone isn't working.

20:47.829 --> 20:49.790
[all panting]

20:54.169 --> 20:56.171
[soft eerie music]

21:01.385 --> 21:03.595
[Arisu] Was there some kind of
evacuation drill today?

21:05.931 --> 21:07.266
[Karube] Not that I know about.

21:09.101 --> 21:12.354
[Chota] Some sort of event?
A flash mob, maybe?

21:13.021 --> 21:15.357
[Karube] The scale of this
is way too big for that.

21:15.440 --> 21:16.566
[Karube sighs]

21:19.361 --> 21:21.738
What if it's only
the three of us left alive?

21:38.380 --> 21:40.590
This doesn't seem all that bad to me.

21:42.134 --> 21:43.093
What?

21:43.176 --> 21:44.678
[chuckles]

21:44.761 --> 21:46.179
Don't you find this exciting?

21:48.432 --> 21:49.808
You out of your mind?

21:49.891 --> 21:51.893
[laughs]

21:51.977 --> 21:54.313
You're right. I think it's kinda cool.

21:54.396 --> 21:55.272
Why?

21:55.939 --> 21:58.233
'Cause I don't have to go to work.
That's good.

21:58.317 --> 21:59.568
[Chota, Arisu laugh]

21:59.651 --> 22:01.069
Are you guys crazy?

22:01.153 --> 22:03.071
No one to be angry with us.

22:03.155 --> 22:05.407
And we can eat and drink
all we want, right?

22:05.490 --> 22:07.034
[laughing]

22:07.117 --> 22:08.702
You'll be a virgin your whole life.

22:09.661 --> 22:12.414
Huh? Don't think I'd like that.

22:15.584 --> 22:18.003
[laughing]

22:27.179 --> 22:29.765
[Arisu echoing]
Any virgins out there?

22:29.848 --> 22:31.099
[Karube] You tryin' to scare 'em?

22:31.183 --> 22:32.934
[Chota laughs]
I'd do it!

22:33.018 --> 22:35.896
[Arisu, Chota whooping]

22:35.979 --> 22:39.107
- [Chota] Isn't this great?
- [Arisu] Awesome! Whoo!

22:39.191 --> 22:40.901
- [Karube] Guys.
- [Chota] Arisu!

22:40.984 --> 22:42.861
- [Arisu, Chota laughing]
- [Karube] Stop joking around, you guys!

22:42.944 --> 22:44.154
- [Chota] Karube!
- [Arisu] Karube!

22:44.237 --> 22:45.530
[laughing]

22:45.614 --> 22:47.032
- That hurts!
- [Karube] Huh?

22:47.115 --> 22:49.117
- [lights clunk, buzz]
- Huh?

22:49.201 --> 22:50.202
[Chota gasps]

22:52.287 --> 22:53.455
Fuck.

23:00.629 --> 23:04.800
WELCOME, PLAYERS
THE GAME WILL COMMENCE IN A MOMENT

23:04.883 --> 23:06.885
[unsettling music]

23:07.844 --> 23:10.555
WELCOME, PLAYERS.
THE GAME WILL COMMENCE IN A MOMENT

23:10.639 --> 23:11.598
[Karube] Game?

23:19.356 --> 23:21.358
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

23:24.653 --> 23:26.113
- Over there.
- Hm?

23:28.115 --> 23:29.324
[Chota] Lights?

23:29.908 --> 23:31.159
[Karube] Somebody must be there.

23:32.744 --> 23:33.662
[breathes nervously]

23:33.745 --> 23:34.830
Let's go.

23:34.913 --> 23:35.789
Okay.

23:37.332 --> 23:39.334
[eerie music]

23:51.721 --> 23:53.723
[panting]

24:09.698 --> 24:11.783
[hissing in distance]

24:11.867 --> 24:18.874
GM BUILDING

24:26.548 --> 24:28.508
[hissing continues]

24:30.927 --> 24:37.350
THE GAME ARENA IS UP AHEAD

24:37.434 --> 24:38.810
[light buzzes]

24:58.747 --> 25:00.749
[foreboding music]

25:19.142 --> 25:21.144
[clock ticking]

25:34.824 --> 25:36.243
[light crackling]

25:36.868 --> 25:39.704
1 PER PERSON

25:51.007 --> 25:53.301
[scanner chiming]

25:53.385 --> 25:55.387
[suspenseful music]

25:58.974 --> 26:02.018
1 PER PERSON

26:18.201 --> 26:21.037
FACE RECOGNITION IN PROGRESS
PLEASE WAIT FOR A MOMENT

26:21.871 --> 26:23.164
It's got face recognition.

26:23.873 --> 26:25.125
Do we use these phones?

26:27.544 --> 26:28.878
[Arisu] There's no signal.

26:28.962 --> 26:31.589
[Chota] The outgoing call function
is disabled.

26:32.090 --> 26:33.049
GAME
PLEASE WAIT

26:33.133 --> 26:35.176
[announcer] Please wait
for the game to commence.

26:35.844 --> 26:38.638
Currently, there are three participants.

26:39.431 --> 26:42.976
One minute remaining
until registration closes.

26:43.059 --> 26:44.561
What the hell is this?

26:46.062 --> 26:47.105
[Shibuki] A game.

26:47.188 --> 26:48.148
[men gasp]

26:48.231 --> 26:51.026
[Chota] Huh… Finally, a person.

26:51.651 --> 26:54.112
Hey. Uh, do you know where everyone went?

26:59.409 --> 27:00.660
[scanner chimes]

27:07.917 --> 27:09.002
[electricity buzzes]

27:09.085 --> 27:10.128
[men gasp]

27:10.211 --> 27:11.296
[crackling]

27:11.379 --> 27:12.881
[Arisu] What the hell was that?

27:13.506 --> 27:14.716
[Chota] A laser?

27:14.799 --> 27:15.633
CHOTA SEGAWA

27:15.717 --> 27:18.470
Cross the borderline,
and you'll never return.

27:18.553 --> 27:19.679
[men shudder]

27:19.763 --> 27:21.806
You have no choice but to play the game.

27:33.276 --> 27:34.319
- Whoa!
- [Karube] Hey!

27:35.111 --> 27:36.571
[breathing heavily]

27:39.240 --> 27:41.368
[Karube] You heard what she said.
Don't do it.

27:41.451 --> 27:42.660
[gasps]

27:46.414 --> 27:47.999
[girl] Oh!

27:48.083 --> 27:49.959
I'm so relieved!

27:50.752 --> 27:53.004
Jeez, I thought there was no one else…

27:53.088 --> 27:55.090
- [men yell]
- [scanner chimes]

27:56.883 --> 27:58.593
[Shibuki] My condolences.

28:01.846 --> 28:03.848
[phones chime melodically]

28:07.310 --> 28:08.937
[announcer] Registration is now closed.

28:09.646 --> 28:11.689
The game will now commence.

28:12.315 --> 28:13.274
Game?

28:14.192 --> 28:16.611
[announcer] Game, "Dead or Alive".

28:16.694 --> 28:17.779
DEAD OR ALIVE

28:17.862 --> 28:20.365
Difficulty, Three of Clubs.

28:20.448 --> 28:22.200
Three of Clubs?

28:22.784 --> 28:23.868
What does that mean?

28:24.744 --> 28:26.204
[announcer] Rule.

28:26.287 --> 28:30.125
Select the correct door
within the stipulated time frame.

28:30.792 --> 28:31.626
What?

28:31.709 --> 28:33.253
[announcer] Clear condition.

28:33.336 --> 28:36.297
Leave the building within the time limit.

28:36.381 --> 28:37.924
LEAVE THE BUILDING
WITHIN THE TIME LIMIT.

28:38.007 --> 28:38.842
[elevator dings]

28:39.509 --> 28:41.428
START

28:41.511 --> 28:43.513
[eerie music]

28:47.100 --> 28:48.810
You'll die if you just stand there.

28:53.189 --> 28:55.191
[suspenseful music]

28:58.111 --> 28:59.320
[Karube] We have no choice.

29:00.447 --> 29:01.531
[sighs]

29:13.793 --> 29:14.711
[elevator dings]

29:18.673 --> 29:20.300
[phones chime]

29:20.383 --> 29:22.093
[announcer] The time limit for this room…

29:22.177 --> 29:23.011
TIME LIMIT

29:23.094 --> 29:24.679
[announcer] …is two minutes.

29:27.265 --> 29:29.267
[suspenseful music]

29:29.350 --> 29:31.519
[clock ticking]

29:39.861 --> 29:40.862
[Karube scoffs]

29:42.489 --> 29:43.656
What is this?

29:50.455 --> 29:51.289
LIVE

29:51.372 --> 29:52.624
[Shibuki] Alive…

29:52.707 --> 29:53.541
DIE

29:53.625 --> 29:54.626
[Shibuki] …or Dead.

29:56.628 --> 29:59.047
Is this really a game?

29:59.130 --> 30:00.215
[giggles]

30:00.298 --> 30:04.135
I think… this is really getting exciting.

30:04.219 --> 30:05.428
[chuckles]

30:08.556 --> 30:11.142
I'm sure this must be
doors to an art gallery.

30:12.852 --> 30:15.939
I want to go… home.

30:16.648 --> 30:19.317
[soft chuckle]
It'll be fine. You're with us.

30:19.400 --> 30:22.237
We'll play the game,
get our prize, and go home. Okay?

30:22.320 --> 30:23.988
- Our prize?
- [Chota chuckles]

30:24.072 --> 30:26.074
- Yeah, I'm sure we're gonna get one.
- [phone chimes]

30:26.157 --> 30:27.617
[announcer] One minute remaining.

30:27.700 --> 30:28.785
Arisu.

30:29.410 --> 30:30.912
Which door do you think it is?

30:30.995 --> 30:32.372
[chuckles]

30:32.956 --> 30:35.875
[Chota] Dead or Alive.

30:35.959 --> 30:38.044
Well, it can't be the skeleton, right?

30:40.213 --> 30:41.589
And if we choose the wrong door?

30:42.674 --> 30:43.925
The answer is "Alive".

30:44.008 --> 30:46.177
Open the door that says "Alive".

30:47.136 --> 30:48.221
How do you know?

30:48.805 --> 30:51.266
Because… obviously, it's the "Alive" door.

30:52.225 --> 30:54.018
[sniffing]

30:54.561 --> 30:55.770
Do you guys smell something?

30:55.854 --> 30:57.939
[sniffs]
Oh, fuck!

30:58.022 --> 31:00.441
- [hissing]
- [all gasping]

31:00.525 --> 31:01.526
[Chota] Is it a fire?

31:01.609 --> 31:02.735
- [coughing]
- [phones chime]

31:02.819 --> 31:05.405
- [announcer] Thirty seconds remaining.
- The answer is "Alive"!

31:05.488 --> 31:07.532
- Hurry and open the door!
- [Karube] Open it yourself!

31:07.615 --> 31:09.284
What'll happen if our time's up?

31:09.367 --> 31:10.994
[Shibuki] We won't get more time. Hurry!

31:11.077 --> 31:12.412
[Arisu] Why do you think
it's the right one?

31:12.495 --> 31:14.789
'Cause we shouldn't
choose the "Dead" door, right?

31:14.873 --> 31:16.165
[announcer] Twenty seconds remaining.

31:16.249 --> 31:18.251
[girl] I can't take it, I can't breathe!

31:20.003 --> 31:21.170
[zapping]

31:22.881 --> 31:23.798
[clattering]

31:28.720 --> 31:31.472
Is… she dead?

31:32.140 --> 31:33.266
[coughs]

31:33.349 --> 31:35.393
[announcer] Ten seconds remaining.

31:35.476 --> 31:37.228
[all coughing]

31:37.312 --> 31:39.188
DIE

31:39.272 --> 31:40.440
[announcer] Five,

31:40.523 --> 31:42.692
four, three, two…

31:42.775 --> 31:44.277
- Chota!
- [announcer] …one.

31:44.903 --> 31:46.696
- Move!
- [blasting]

31:46.779 --> 31:47.989
[Karube yelps]

31:48.072 --> 31:49.657
[announcer] The time limit for this room

31:49.741 --> 31:51.993
is one minute and fifty seconds.

31:52.076 --> 31:53.620
[timer chimes]

31:54.245 --> 31:56.247
[panting heavily]

31:57.290 --> 31:58.958
She really is dead.

31:59.042 --> 32:00.335
[Arisu] What the hell is this?

32:01.210 --> 32:04.047
[panting]
You were the one who killed that girl.

32:04.130 --> 32:06.549
But you guys survived
because of me, didn't you?

32:06.633 --> 32:07.467
What?

32:07.550 --> 32:08.843
[Shibuki] Blame me all you want.

32:08.927 --> 32:11.095
If you guys don't think fast,
you're gonna die too.

32:13.181 --> 32:14.349
[Karube] Damn it!

32:14.432 --> 32:15.266
[breathing heavily]

32:15.350 --> 32:17.644
[Karube] Do we choose
the "Die" door now, huh?

32:17.727 --> 32:20.980
Since the last one was "Die"
the next one should be "Live".

32:21.064 --> 32:23.358
Yeah, but maybe
that's what they want us to think.

32:23.441 --> 32:26.152
- But it's hard to choose "Die".
- [Shibuki] Wait a second.

32:26.235 --> 32:29.614
I think that this is a game
where we choose a sacrifice.

32:29.697 --> 32:30.573
A sacrifice?

32:30.657 --> 32:32.742
There's probably no difference
in the doors.

32:32.825 --> 32:34.494
What's important is who opens them.

32:34.577 --> 32:37.413
They want us to choose a person
within the time limit.

32:37.497 --> 32:39.082
You sacrificed that girl.

32:39.832 --> 32:41.334
Why don't you open the next door?

32:41.417 --> 32:44.462
[Shibuki] Because I believe if I survive,
it'll be for the good of all mankind.

32:44.545 --> 32:46.965
- Well, don't we feel good about ourselves?
- [retches]

32:47.048 --> 32:48.341
[groaning]

32:48.424 --> 32:50.176
[announcer] One minute has passed.

32:51.135 --> 32:53.137
[dire music]

32:53.221 --> 32:55.348
No one will open a door at this rate.

32:55.431 --> 32:57.350
We're all gonna die in the fire
if time runs out!

32:57.433 --> 32:58.893
Then why don't you open it?

32:58.977 --> 32:59.811
[gasps]

32:59.894 --> 33:01.813
[Shibuki] You want me to open it,
why don't you do it yourself?

33:01.896 --> 33:03.439
You want someone else to open it!

33:03.523 --> 33:05.650
[all coughing]

33:11.239 --> 33:12.407
All right, I'll open it.

33:12.490 --> 33:13.616
[Karube coughing]

33:16.244 --> 33:17.078
Arisu!

33:17.161 --> 33:18.830
LIVE

33:19.956 --> 33:21.249
DIE

33:23.584 --> 33:25.503
Stop, Arisu. Don't listen to her!

33:27.588 --> 33:29.048
I'll open the door, fuck!

33:29.132 --> 33:31.134
[suspenseful music]

33:32.760 --> 33:35.096
[Arisu shuddering]

33:39.350 --> 33:41.102
[announcer] Thirty seconds remaining.

33:41.185 --> 33:43.187
[suspenseful music continues]

33:48.568 --> 33:49.485
Arisu!

33:55.658 --> 33:56.909
[breathes shakily]

33:58.661 --> 34:01.122
[sobbing]

34:01.205 --> 34:04.125
See? Not so easy, is it?

34:04.208 --> 34:06.294
Even you would have sacrificed that girl!

34:06.377 --> 34:08.046
- Shut the fuck up!
- [phone chimes]

34:08.129 --> 34:09.881
[announcer] Twenty seconds remaining.

34:10.923 --> 34:12.300
I'll do it.

34:12.383 --> 34:13.885
He's not very lucky, anyway.

34:13.968 --> 34:16.054
- [Arisu] Karube!
- [Karube] We'll take turns.

34:19.223 --> 34:20.433
You'll go after me.

34:21.309 --> 34:22.810
[announcer] Ten seconds remaining.

34:23.311 --> 34:24.145
Karube.

34:25.897 --> 34:27.315
[grunts]

34:28.441 --> 34:29.609
Karube!

34:31.861 --> 34:32.945
- [gasps]
- [announcer] Five,

34:33.029 --> 34:34.947
- four, three…
- Karube!

34:35.031 --> 34:36.657
- [announcer] …two, one.
- [Shibuki] Hurry!

34:37.241 --> 34:39.243
[flames blasting]

34:40.661 --> 34:42.663
[announcer] The time limit for this room

34:42.747 --> 34:44.832
is one minute and forty seconds.

34:44.916 --> 34:45.958
[timer chimes]

34:46.042 --> 34:47.835
The time limit is shortening.

34:47.919 --> 34:49.545
[sobs]
I can't do this anymore.

34:49.629 --> 34:51.589
We're taking turns.
[panting]

34:51.672 --> 34:52.965
You open the door next.

34:53.049 --> 34:54.133
[breathing shakily]

34:55.718 --> 34:57.887
- [Karube] I'll choose the door.
- Wait.

34:57.970 --> 34:59.972
- [Shibuki whimpers]
- [Karube] Go ahead and open.

35:00.056 --> 35:01.182
Open it!

35:01.265 --> 35:02.308
[sobs]

35:02.391 --> 35:03.476
I can't.

35:04.143 --> 35:05.228
[sighs deeply]

35:06.896 --> 35:08.981
[panting]

35:09.065 --> 35:11.275
Arisu, what do you think?

35:11.859 --> 35:12.902
Think?

35:13.486 --> 35:16.239
You always say there are solutions
built into every game, right?

35:16.322 --> 35:18.574
- But this isn't a game.
- You can figure it out.

35:18.658 --> 35:21.661
You've always solved the puzzle games
that I could never figure out.

35:21.744 --> 35:24.580
- So do it!
- Karube, this is not a game.

35:25.123 --> 35:26.332
It's all about luck.

35:26.415 --> 35:28.668
- Arisu, just think!
- [announcer] One minute has passed.

35:29.544 --> 35:31.003
Was there a clue somewhere?

35:31.921 --> 35:34.882
Think back.
Together, we came into this building…

35:34.966 --> 35:36.175
Remember the time limit!

35:36.259 --> 35:38.427
- And then, we went into the elevator--
- I won't do this!

35:38.511 --> 35:40.763
Don't give up, Arisu!
You can reboot this game!

35:40.847 --> 35:42.348
It's impossible, I'm telling you!

35:42.431 --> 35:44.517
- We're going to die.
- You're the gamer!

35:44.600 --> 35:47.645
While I was working my ass off,
you were sitting on a couch playing! Huh?

35:47.728 --> 35:49.063
You think that makes you better?

35:49.147 --> 35:50.940
The only thing you really know
is how to fight.

35:51.023 --> 35:53.067
- How is that better?
- Yeah? Well, I'll show you how.

35:53.151 --> 35:54.944
Stop it, Karube!

35:55.486 --> 35:57.071
[sobbing]

35:57.155 --> 35:58.656
GM BUILDING

35:58.739 --> 36:00.032
Wait.

36:02.869 --> 36:03.786
Wait a minute.

36:04.787 --> 36:06.706
- Are you okay, Arisu?
- [shushes]

36:11.127 --> 36:13.129
[announcer] Thirty seconds remaining.

36:13.212 --> 36:15.047
[Arisu panting]

36:18.843 --> 36:20.261
BMW 523.

36:20.344 --> 36:21.220
Huh?

36:21.804 --> 36:23.264
It was a BMW 523.

36:23.890 --> 36:25.057
Yeah?

36:28.936 --> 36:30.021
The answer is "Die".

36:30.605 --> 36:32.732
- How do you know?
- [announcer] Ten seconds remaining.

36:32.815 --> 36:34.150
We gotta hurry!

36:34.233 --> 36:35.610
I'll open it up.

36:35.693 --> 36:38.487
Arisu! Are you sure the answer is "Die"?

36:38.571 --> 36:39.447
Please…

36:39.530 --> 36:40.406
[announcer] Five,

36:40.489 --> 36:41.741
- four…
- [screams]

36:41.824 --> 36:42.825
[announcer] …three…

36:42.909 --> 36:44.160
- This means I'm right!
- [announcer] …two…

36:44.243 --> 36:45.536
- [Karube roars]
- [announcer] …one.

36:45.620 --> 36:47.580
[flames blast]

36:47.663 --> 36:49.916
- [grunting]
- [announcer] The time limit for this room

36:49.999 --> 36:52.418
- is one minute and thirty seconds.
- [Chota] Where to next?

36:52.501 --> 36:53.920
Do you know which one this time?

36:55.004 --> 36:58.299
My father has a BMW 523.
It's 4 meters, 94 centimeters.

36:58.382 --> 37:00.384
One of 'em
was parked beside the building.

37:00.927 --> 37:03.095
[upbeat music]

37:03.179 --> 37:05.723
[Arisu] The length of the building
is equivalent to four of those cars.

37:05.806 --> 37:09.352
This means that the building
is approximately 24 meters in length.

37:09.435 --> 37:12.855
And this room… If I measure with my feet,

37:12.939 --> 37:15.358
One, two, three…

37:17.401 --> 37:19.153
It should be around six meters.

37:20.363 --> 37:21.822
According to the evacuation map,

37:21.906 --> 37:23.908
the elevator
is at the corner of the building.

37:24.742 --> 37:25.993
1F EVACUATION ROUTE MAP

37:27.495 --> 37:29.413
[Arisu] The shape of the building
is square.

37:30.248 --> 37:31.874
This room is also square-shaped.

37:33.376 --> 37:35.336
Assuming that one side
of the building is 20 meters

37:35.419 --> 37:38.130
and the length of a single room
is 6 meters, that's three rooms a side.

37:38.214 --> 37:39.548
[announcer] One minute has passed.

37:39.632 --> 37:41.133
- I need something to write on!
- Uh…

37:41.217 --> 37:43.052
- Here.
- Here, here, here, here, here.

37:43.135 --> 37:45.346
[pants, grunts]

37:45.429 --> 37:46.973
We're in a square building.

37:47.056 --> 37:49.308
Assuming that each room is square,

37:49.392 --> 37:51.644
this means that this floor has nine rooms.

37:51.727 --> 37:54.063
- It's just like a puzzle.
- Arisu's a genius at them.

37:54.146 --> 37:55.606
We started from this room.

37:56.399 --> 37:57.858
The high-school girl died…

37:57.942 --> 37:59.902
- [Chota coughing]
- [Arisu] …in this room.

37:59.986 --> 38:02.530
Thanks to Karube, we moved forward.

38:02.613 --> 38:05.241
This means that the door to the right
cannot be accessed.

38:05.324 --> 38:07.326
Then I opened the door to this room.

38:07.410 --> 38:09.036
[announcer] Thirty seconds remaining.

38:09.120 --> 38:12.331
By process of elimination, this room
and the one beside it can't be accessed.

38:12.415 --> 38:13.374
I'm sure of that.

38:13.457 --> 38:14.875
[announcer] Ten seconds remaining.

38:14.959 --> 38:15.960
The answer is "Dead"!

38:16.043 --> 38:17.545
The "Alive" door is a trap!

38:17.628 --> 38:19.880
Four, three, two…

38:19.964 --> 38:21.424
- [all yelping]
- [announcer] …one.

38:21.507 --> 38:23.467
[flames blasting]

38:24.051 --> 38:26.178
- [panting]
- [announcer] The time limit for this room

38:26.262 --> 38:28.055
is one minute and twenty seconds.

38:28.139 --> 38:30.057
If your reasoning is right,
we're gonna survive!

38:30.766 --> 38:31.809
You're awesome, Arisu!

38:32.560 --> 38:35.688
[Arisu] This game is not based on luck.
We need to clear it together!

38:35.771 --> 38:36.939
According to my drawing,

38:37.023 --> 38:39.108
- the next is also "Dead".
- Let's do it!

38:39.191 --> 38:40.192
Ah!

38:40.276 --> 38:42.278
[exciting music]

38:42.361 --> 38:44.280
- Ready?
- [Shibuki, Karube, Chota] Uh-huh.

38:47.158 --> 38:49.285
- [Karube] Nice!
- [laughter]

38:49.368 --> 38:50.328
[Chota] Yeah, we did it!

38:50.411 --> 38:52.663
- [announcer] The time limit for this room…
- [Karube] What's next? Huh? Huh?

38:52.747 --> 38:54.081
[announcer] …is one minute
and ten seconds.

38:54.165 --> 38:56.542
[exciting music continues]

38:56.625 --> 38:58.044
"Alive".

39:01.088 --> 39:01.922
Let's go.

39:02.548 --> 39:03.382
[Arisu yelps]

39:03.966 --> 39:06.677
[men cheering, laughing]

39:06.761 --> 39:08.971
- [Chota] Hey, that hurts!
- Huh?

39:09.055 --> 39:11.140
[announcer] The time limit for this room
is one minute.

39:11.223 --> 39:12.725
[Karube, Chota cheering]

39:12.808 --> 39:14.060
There's no door here.

39:14.143 --> 39:16.270
- [Karube] All right!
- [Chota] Oh, yeah! Oh, yeah!

39:16.354 --> 39:18.189
- That hurts!
- [Karube] Take this!

39:19.648 --> 39:20.900
So what's next?

39:28.074 --> 39:29.909
[Chota] Since that door
is out of the question,

39:29.992 --> 39:31.535
should we choose one on the outer wall?

39:34.080 --> 39:35.706
- Wait a second!
- [gasps]

39:36.290 --> 39:39.293
- I might just have missed something.
- [announcer] Fifty seconds remaining.

39:42.338 --> 39:43.714
[Arisu] The room we're in right now

39:43.798 --> 39:46.133
is on the left-end corner of the building.

39:46.675 --> 39:49.470
The clearing condition
is to leave this building.

39:50.137 --> 39:52.848
That's why we'd feel we should
choose the "Dead" door to lead us out.

39:52.932 --> 39:56.018
But as I recall, there is no gap
between this and the adjoining building.

39:56.102 --> 39:58.687
The "Alive" door will lead us
to where the high school girl died.

39:59.355 --> 40:02.191
I don't know why there's no door
to connect to the back of the building.

40:03.234 --> 40:04.735
I must have overlooked something,

40:04.819 --> 40:05.945
but what?

40:06.529 --> 40:09.448
There shouldn't be any space left
for them to create a trap.

40:10.199 --> 40:11.409
And if that's the case…

40:11.492 --> 40:13.494
[suspenseful music]

40:15.996 --> 40:18.249
We're wasting time! We're all gonna die!

40:18.332 --> 40:19.542
You haven't even opened a door!

40:19.625 --> 40:21.752
What are you even talking about?
Don't blame this on me!

40:21.836 --> 40:23.337
- [Shibuki coughing]
- [Chota] Stop it, you two!

40:23.421 --> 40:24.964
- Wait…
- [Chota] Wait!

40:25.047 --> 40:27.174
Chota, you took a video of the first room!

40:27.258 --> 40:28.926
There's no time for that!

40:29.009 --> 40:30.594
[announcer] Thirty seconds remaining.

40:30.678 --> 40:32.096
[Arisu] I could've missed something.

40:32.179 --> 40:33.514
[Chota] …doors to an art gallery.

40:34.640 --> 40:36.434
[Karube] Which door do you think it is?

40:36.517 --> 40:39.019
[breathing heavily]

40:39.103 --> 40:40.104
[Karube] Ah, fuck!

40:40.729 --> 40:42.481
[Chota] What'll happen if our time's up?

40:42.565 --> 40:44.191
[girl] I can't take it,
I can't breathe!

40:44.775 --> 40:46.193
[Arisu shuddering]

40:49.447 --> 40:51.240
- [Arisu] There's no door!
- Huh?

40:51.323 --> 40:53.367
There's no door in the room
the girl entered!

40:53.451 --> 40:54.535
- What does that mean?
- There's a door here!

40:54.618 --> 40:57.163
- [announcer] Ten seconds remain.
- [Arisu] That means…

40:57.246 --> 40:58.831
The room the high-school girl died
isn't next to us!

40:58.914 --> 41:00.166
You mean what?

41:00.249 --> 41:01.917
There's another room on the other side!

41:02.001 --> 41:04.795
- [Shibuki whimpers]
- [announcer] Three, two, one.

41:04.879 --> 41:06.213
[Arisu grunts]

41:06.297 --> 41:08.215
[screams]

41:09.300 --> 41:12.928
[announcer] The time limit for this room
is ten seconds.

41:13.012 --> 41:14.138
Ten seconds?

41:14.221 --> 41:15.598
- Are you kidding?
- [Chota screaming]

41:15.681 --> 41:17.308
It's not "Alive"! It's "Dead"!

41:17.391 --> 41:19.101
Don't open it, it's a trap!

41:19.185 --> 41:20.853
[announcer] Five, four,

41:20.936 --> 41:22.271
- three…
- Hurry!

41:22.354 --> 41:24.565
- [announcer] …two, one.
- [screaming]

41:24.648 --> 41:26.942
[flames blast]

41:29.570 --> 41:32.239
- [all panting]
- [Shibuki] Which way now?

41:32.323 --> 41:33.782
[Arisu] Head downstairs!

41:33.866 --> 41:37.578
[all panting]

41:37.661 --> 41:39.246
[Karube] C'mon, Chota. You can do it.

41:40.706 --> 41:43.042
[panting continues]

41:48.172 --> 41:50.174
[groans]

41:51.759 --> 41:53.469
- [grunting]
- [phones chime]

41:53.552 --> 41:55.304
[announcer] Game cleared.

41:55.387 --> 41:56.222
GAME CLEARED

41:56.305 --> 41:57.515
[announcer] Congratulations.

41:57.598 --> 42:00.601
[all panting]

42:01.185 --> 42:03.354
- [Chota grunting]
- It's all thanks to you.

42:03.437 --> 42:04.605
[breathing heavily]

42:05.189 --> 42:06.565
Thank you.

42:12.029 --> 42:13.364
[Chota] It's my karma.

42:13.447 --> 42:14.532
[all panting]

42:16.951 --> 42:19.495
[groans in pain]

42:21.455 --> 42:23.457
[breathing heavily]

42:36.512 --> 42:38.681
[Chota grunting]

42:40.182 --> 42:42.184
[eerie music]

42:44.436 --> 42:46.438
[Chota grunting]

42:57.992 --> 42:59.451
[phone chimes]

43:00.536 --> 43:04.039
[announcer] To the survivors of the game,
we will now supply you with a visa.

43:04.123 --> 43:07.251
WE WILL SUPPLY ALL GAME SURVIVORS
WITH A 3-DAY VISA

43:08.127 --> 43:09.420
Visa?

43:11.422 --> 43:14.008
[footsteps approaching]

43:23.726 --> 43:24.977
I'm going to

43:25.519 --> 43:26.937
drop out of the game!

43:29.440 --> 43:33.402
Listen. There's no end to the game,
no matter how much you clear.

43:37.072 --> 43:39.116
My visa just ended today.

43:39.199 --> 43:40.743
[breathing heavily]

43:40.826 --> 43:42.286
And now…

43:44.163 --> 43:45.956
I wish to play no longer.

43:47.583 --> 43:48.834
[zapping]

43:51.503 --> 43:53.505
[ominous music]

43:55.507 --> 43:57.009
GM BUILDING

43:57.092 --> 43:58.510
[lights buzz out]

43:59.970 --> 44:01.972
[suspenseful music]

44:23.369 --> 44:24.745
When your visa expires,

44:25.663 --> 44:27.623
you must return to the game or…

44:29.875 --> 44:32.211
Our visas will end too.

44:33.337 --> 44:34.588
We've got three days.

44:35.089 --> 44:36.590
If you don't want to die,

44:37.299 --> 44:39.385
you'll have to continue playing the game.

44:45.474 --> 44:47.476
[dire music]

44:55.234 --> 44:59.363
[lasers zapping, rumbling]

45:07.037 --> 45:09.498
[zapping continues]

45:15.254 --> 45:17.256
[dire music builds]

45:33.105 --> 45:35.107
[closing theme music]

45:45.534 --> 45:47.953
BASED ON THE ORIGINAL GRAPHIC NOVEL
ALICE IN BORDERLAND BY HARO ASO
